# 1. Project Release
Release V1.0

# 2. Date
2026-07-14

# 3. Change Control
Issue Date | Version | Details | Author
---|---|---|---
2026-07-14 | 1.0 | Initial strategy for AD-488 (Jira API 401 Unauthorized) | QA Director

# 4. Scope
## 4.1 In Scope
- Jira API authentication validation
- Error handling for unauthorized access

## 4.2 Out of Scope
- Functional testing of AD-488 requirements (not available)
- Any features dependent on Jira requirement content

# 5. Quality Objectives
- Validate Jira API authentication
- Verify error handling for missing or inaccessible issues

# 6. Test Approach
## 6.1 Testing Levels
- API / Service Integration Level (Jira API authentication and response validation)
- Application Error-Handling Level (consumer handling of unauthorized and missing issue responses)
- End-to-End Integration Level (request-to-error-surface workflow for inaccessible Jira issues)

## 6.2 Testing Types
- Functional Testing
- Negative Testing
- Integration Testing
- Regression Testing

## 6.3 Test Design Techniques
- Error Guessing (authentication failure and inaccessible resource scenarios)
- Equivalence Partitioning (authorized vs unauthorized vs inaccessible request classes)
- Decision Table Testing (mapping response conditions such as valid auth, invalid auth, and missing description to expected system handling)
- State/Response Transition Testing (request outcome transitions from request initiation to 401 handling and user-visible error state)

# 7. Test Environments
- Integration/Staging environment with Jira API connectivity configuration
- Mock/stub Jira service capable of returning 401 Unauthorized and missing-field payloads
- Test credentials matrix covering valid, invalid, expired, and absent authentication tokens
- Log/trace capture facilities to verify error propagation, masking, and observability

