# 14. Tools Table
Tool | Purpose
---|---
PyTest | API authentication and error handling validation
JMeter | Simulating SLA clock breaches and load
OWASP ZAP | Security testing for unauthorized access
tcconfig | Network condition simulation (e.g., latency, drops)

# 15. Test Schedule / Milestone
- Test design: 2 days
- Environment setup: 1 day
- Script development: 2 days
- Execution: 2 days
- Reporting: 1 day
**Total duration:** 8 working days
**Resources:** 1 QA Automation Engineer, 1 Test Lead

# 16. Assumptions
- Test environments and credentials are available
- Mock/stub Jira API endpoints can be configured
- Required tools (PyTest, JMeter, OWASP ZAP, tcconfig) are accessible

# 17. Risk Mitigation Table
Risk Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation Action
---|---|---|---
Dynamic Jira API endpoint changes | High | Medium | Use environment variables and config-driven endpoints; validate before each run
Authentication token expiry during test window | Medium | High | Automate token refresh and monitor expiry logs
Network instability (e.g., connection drops) | Medium | Medium | Use tcconfig to simulate and handle network faults in test runs
SLA processing latency in error propagation | Medium | Medium | Use JMeter to simulate load and measure error response times
Missing or delayed test environment provisioning | High | Low | Pre-schedule environment setup and validate readiness before test execution

